WEBVTT

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:02.630
Extra speed leaves fewer

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:03.150
options.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.890
In a heavy truck, staying

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.510
in control starts with noticing

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:07.960
your speed before the road

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:08.710
changes ahead.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.470
The posted limit is a

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:11.850
maximum.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:12.630
Rain,

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:13.390
traffic,

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.110
curves, or poor visibility can

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:17.130
make that speed unsafe,

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.250
even when other vehicles pass

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:19.550
you.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.290
Check your speed as conditions

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:22.730
change.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:23.970
Ease off early,

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.990
then slow smoothly before a

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.310
lower limit, a queue,

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:28.770
or the next curve ahead.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.430
Protect your following space.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.610
After another vehicle enters the

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:34.870
gap,

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:36.930
ease off gently and rebuild

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.450
a safe buffer while remaining

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:38.890
in lane.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:42.260
Running late does not change

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.030
safe speed.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.720
If conditions delay the trip,

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:46.590
park safely before updating

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.170
dispatch and agree on a

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:48.990
realistic arrival.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.170
Carry three actions into your

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.760
next trip: observe changing

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:54.270
conditions,

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:56.590
reduce speed early, and preserve

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.230
following space before the next

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:58.900
hazard develops.
